# Solve-side interactive tmux debug runtime audit

- [ ] Never import or modify absorb-side code or runtime assets.
- [ ] Use tmux multi-argument direct execution; never interpolate task/prompt text into a shell command.
- [ ] Every attempt has a private tmux socket, session, workspace, model UID, config and export.
- [ ] `INTERACTIVE_TMUX_DEBUG` is recorded as development-only by default.
- [ ] Pane capture and health snapshots are append-only.
- [ ] Every sent key is allowlisted and recorded as an intervention.
- [ ] DONE never triggers an immediate kill; sealing requires a dead pane and export inspection.
- [ ] Missing output, invalid DONE, missing export and model mismatch remain visible.
- [ ] Finalize never overwrites an existing output bundle.
- [ ] Abort is explicit, attributed and sealed as `ABORTED`; it never masquerades as finalize success.
